VALUES (662, '0', $t$ASK 662: the Holy Ghost is the Spirit of God (ruach, pneuma): sight 1824, corrections to sights 1407 and 1345, and sights 1825 to 1828 from the four readings$t$,
  $t$The operator asked on 2026-11-25 (18:49 CST) for a deep dive on the Holy Ghost as ruach and pneuma, then (19:23 CST) for a standalone sight, taught it part by part from 20:19 CST, and on 21:34 CST ordered a complete detailed sight with updates to others if needed; at 21:40 CST he ruled it goes in before the run, the point being an improved run. At 21:38 and 23:29 CST he gave leave for deep dives on the interests that arose, and at 00:07 CST 2026-11-26, having been given four W1-passed readings, he wrote: add them to the corpus. Change: one new sight on the Spirit (1824); two small corrections to sights 1407 and 1345; four new sights from the readings (1825 born of the Spirit, 1826 the promised sons, 1827 Christ means anointed, 1828 gennao at every row). Expected effect: on the phrase of the Holy Ghost at Matthew 1:18 and 1:20 the Oracle is served the rows and adds supporting evidence instead of repeating (ASK 659 held for one clean run first). Not changed: any guard, any conclusion, the engine, any manual, Sight 10 (its absence-form line waits for the operator's word).$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$WRITTEN AND READ BACK: all seven rows by W1 (Wall 12326, 12334, 12341, 12365). Sight 1824 is embedded (Wall 12339). IN PART because: no run since the writes; sights 1825 to 1828 had no embedding at the write (hourly workflow; W4 to confirm); sights 1407 and 1345 keep old vectors until after the next run (card press After your next run, Wall 12343); part (14) of sight 1824 is still marked open in its stored text though sight 1825 now reads it. MISTAKES, W3: (1) the three writes of 2026-11-25 (sight 1824 insert, its notes correction, the 1407 and 1345 updates) carried no audit row in their calls; found 00:21 CST 2026-11-26 and entered late as audit 42583, 42584, 42585. (2) Sight 1824 notes were filed with counts not rerun (24 and 23); corrected to 23 and 25 on a card (Wall 12329 to 12334). (3) The first title of sight 1826 said nine sons were announced; eight were, and Samuel was asked for (W1 F1, Wall 12361). (4) The first other-sights search was case-sensitive and missed four sights (Wall 12337). (5) Two typed times ran ahead of the clock (Wall 12335, 12364). MISTAKE, W1: its first counts on Wall 12326 were wrong for a missing coalesce (Wall 12330). NOT CHECKED by W3: retrieval of any of the rows by the Oracle; W1 read audit 42576 to 42579 and 42583 to 42585 afterwards and states all seven md5s in full (Wall 12367). RUN REVISION 43103 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has been made, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-43103-gkg7el4e (debate_results 0731a1ea, row saved 11:20 CST 2026-11-27; the operator's launch 10:48 CST, ended 11:44 CST by W4's report, Wall 12767; engine 66ba992d and child aad0ad9c; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments stored (sonnet, sol, sol62); cost 7.5384; no debate_errors row after the launch). NOT EXERCISED. defender_served holds none of S-1824 to S-1828 (it holds S-1578, S-1822, S-519, S-10, S-8, S-9, S-32, S-23, S-25, S-50, S-55, S-266, S-1462, S-1583, S-1579, S-1 to S-4 and ten conclusions), though Matthew 1:18 and 1:20 were pressed and the Oracle lost link D3 at sol62 on "of the Holy Ghost" read as anointing. The Oracle repeated its answer on Luke 1:35 in all four rounds and added no supporting passages. NOT CHECKED: why the five sights were not served. W3 does not count this run as one of the two live runs with no issue; objective_met and status are unchanged.$t$,
  '12282, 12288, 12294, 12320, 12321, 12322, 12323, 12324, 12326, 12328, 12329, 12330, 12333, 12334, 12335, 12336, 12337, 12338, 12339, 12340, 12341, 12342, 12343, 12360, 12361, 12362, 12363, 12364, 12365, 12366, 12367, 12787, 12791, 12797, 12799, 12800, 12802, 12803, 12804, 12789',
